00:04:06.581 --> 00:04:09.321
China is testing rare Earth, cis-butadiene rubber.

00:04:09.321 --> 00:04:14.741
A synthetic rubber grade meant for electric vehicle or EV tires and heavy duty tires.

00:04:15.261 --> 00:04:20.941
And the South China Morning Post recorded market data quoting the new grade at 22,500 yuan

00:04:20.941 --> 00:04:26.781
per tonne, against 16,660 yuan for conventional rubber in Shandong Province.

00:04:27.161 --> 00:04:32.501
That is a clear premium over ordinary synthetic rubber, and manufacturers are now evaluating

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:36.861
commercial performance as they test whether the material can expand China's place in

00:04:36.861 --> 00:04:37.981
the EV supply chain.

00:04:37.981 --> 00:04:43.201
The higher price is the commercial hurdle, the grade has to prove itself on tires before

00:04:43.201 --> 00:04:46.261
the extra cost becomes a standard line in the factory budget.

